<title>UK: Santer sees risk of &quot;impatience&quot; with UK over EMU.</title>
<headline>Santer sees risk of &quot;impatience&quot; with UK over EMU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer said in an interview with the Times on Friday there was a risk Britain's European Union partners could grow impatient with its indecision over joining a single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a risk,&quot; the Times quoted him as saying. &quot;There could be a certain impatience among the others. I don't know how the United Kingdom is going to react at that moment, but the UK has always said it did not want to leave the European Union.&quot;</p>
<p>The newspaper said Santer predicted Britain would eventually join European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) &quot;regardless of the colour of the next government&quot;.</p>
